{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_4-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_04_420132660", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The article claims that Sam Panopoulos invented the Hawaiian pizza in 1962.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_33_665346040#0_1391306334", "msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_752837630#5_951573945"]}, {"text": "Sam Panopoulos left Greece for Canada in 1954 and opened a restaurant called the Satellite in Chatham, Ontario.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_50_2185395436#1_3005673737"]}, {"text": "In 1962, Panopoulos added canned pineapple to a pizza, creating what is now known as the Hawaiian pizza.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_17_1448273400#0_1598351114"]}, {"text": "The article mentions that Sam Panopoulos can take credit for inventing one of the most popular pizzas in the world: the Hawaiian pizza.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_50_2185395436#6_3005680383"]}, {"text": "However, there is no evidence provided within the article to support the specific year (1962) or other details of this invention.", "citations": []}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_4-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_06_1440134319", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "Instant noodles are high in fat, salt, and calories, which can contribute to weight gain and other health issues.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_06_1439512529#0_2017885596"]}, {"text": "TBHQ is a chemical preservative found in instant noodles that can be toxic in large doses.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_07_625347531#1_1093628578"]}, {"text": "Studies have shown that prolonged exposure to high doses of TBHQ may be carcinogenic, though some studies suggest it could prevent cancer.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_49_1601897982#2_3353303726"]}, {"text": "A study published in The Journal of Nutrition found that eating instant noodles is linked to stroke, diabetes, and heart conditions.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_37_589513295#5_1266775931"]}, {"text": "Women who ate more than two portions of instant noodles per week had a higher chance of developing metabolic syndrome, which is linked to heart conditions and diabetes.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_37_589513295#5_1266775931"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_4-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_08_300872161", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "Coca-Cola once contained cocaine as an ingredient, which was removed in 1903.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_53_418820865#2_837997214"]}, {"text": "The claim that Coca-Cola was involved in CIA drug trafficking operations lacks concrete evidence and appears to be a conspiracy theory without credible backing.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_31_55792397#7_138715782", "msmarco_v2.1_doc_14_549313134#8_1129090048"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_4-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_15_116067546", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "Quantum computers could pose a threat to Bitcoin's security by using algorithms like Grover's and Shor's to crack the encryption of cryptocurrencies.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_355488050#2_764345749"]}, {"text": "An adversary could insert its own blocks and undermine the entire blockchain using a powerful enough quantum computer, according to Rob Campbell from Med Cybersecurity.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_355488050#2_764345749"]}, {"text": "Andersen Cheng, CEO of Post-Quantum, suggests that a practical quantum computer capable of cracking Bitcoin's code could be available within two years based on intelligence community evidence.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_355488050#2_764345749"]}, {"text": "Quantum computers pose a threat to Bitcoin's security by potentially breaking the cryptographic protocols used in its transactions, such as those based on Shor and Grover's algorithms.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_355488050#2_764345749"]}, {"text": "The National Institute for Standards and Technology (NIST) is running a competition to create post-quantum cryptographic algorithms that could secure blockchains against quantum computers.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_355488050#2_764345749"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_4-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_21_861891150", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The 'Satan Shoes' are promoted as each including one drop of actual human blood.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_181289058#2_375784928", "msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_103285033#3_207042049"]}, {"text": "Nike is suing MSCHF over trademark infringement, false designation of origin/unfair competition, trademark dilution, and common law trademark infringement.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_181289058#2_375784928", "msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_103285033#3_207042049"]}, {"text": "MSCHF sold Jesus-themed shoes in 2019, which were also a special design of the Nike Air Max 97 trainers.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_181289058#2_375784928", "msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_103285033#3_207042049"]}, {"text": "Lil Nas X has tweeted in response to some outraged posts about the shoes, including retweeting a message expressing his perspective on the controversy.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_181289058#2_375784928", "msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_103285033#3_207042049"]}, {"text": "Some people online are doubting the shoes' authenticity and think this might be an early April Fool's joke.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_181289058#2_375784928", "msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_103285033#3_207042049"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_4-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_22_1648697797", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The initial claims about Armie Hammer's alleged cannibalistic behavior first surfaced on January 11, 2021.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_53_249113824#6_450713714"]}, {"text": "@houseofeffie shared direct messages that allegedly contain evidence of Armie Hammer's cannibalistic behavior, but their authenticity is not confirmed by any external sources.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_53_249113824#6_450713714"]}, {"text": "Effie, the woman who shared direct messages with @houseofeffie, is not explicitly identified in the provided text. Her identity remains unknown.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_53_249113824#6_450713714"]}, {"text": "Before the alleged cannibalistic behavior claims emerged, Armie Hammer was set to start filming for Shotgun Wedding alongside Jennifer Lopez.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_1192013567#1_2436953508"]}, {"text": "As of now, there are no formal charges or investigations launched against Armie Hammer regarding the alleged cannibalistic behavior claims.", "citations": []}, {"text": "Several of Armie Hammer's exes have come forward with their own comments, suggesting that there might be multiple sources corroborating similar claims.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_53_249113824#6_450713714"]}, {"text": "Supporters of Armie Hammer argue that his explicit comments in Playboy were a result of drinking during the interview, while critics believe these comments reflect his true nature and behavior.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_1192013567#1_2436953508"]}, {"text": "The alleged cannibalistic behavior claims have affected Armie Hammer's relationships, particularly with his ex-wife Elizabeth Chambers. He stated that he cannot leave his children for four months to shoot a film in the Dominican Republic due to these allegations.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_1192013567#1_2436953508"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_4-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_25_481628070", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "President Biden has issued an Executive Order calling for a comprehensive review of federal environmental regulations to address the climate crisis.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_45_67165665#1_151110223"]}, {"text": "The Biden-Harris Administration has set ambitious goals of achieving net-zero emissions by 2050 and a carbon pollution-free power sector by 2035.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_1340334981#0_1515549032"]}, {"text": "President Biden has signed Executive Orders and issued a Presidential Memorandum on scientific integrity to address the climate crisis, create jobs, and restore scientific integrity across federal government.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_32_724920073#3_1349882956"]}, {"text": "The Biden administration announced that roughly 39 million American families will begin receiving direct cash payments in July under a new child benefit created by Democrats' coronavirus relief bill.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_1779407915#0_1992282805"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_4-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_25_501708725", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The article discusses an attempt by Generation Z to cancel Eminem, with millennials defending him on social media.", "citations": []}, {"text": "In a viral TikTok clip, a millennial defends Eminem's lyrics, stating that he was around before Gen Z members were born.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_51_302147394#4_685391415"]}, {"text": "The article mentions that some of Eminem's older hits, such as 'Superman' and 'Guilty Conscience', depict violent themes.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_26_603633527#7_1145159414"]}, {"text": "Rihanna has stated that one of Eminem's verses in 'Love the Way You Lie' was a condemnation, not celebration, of domestic abuse.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_51_302147394#0_685381725"]}, {"text": "The article notes that more powerful figures have tried and failed to cancel Eminem, including former presidents George Bush and Donald Trump.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_30_1602761268#0_3398195126"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_4-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_25_502424913", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The US government is reportedly gearing up to share information about the 'reality' of UFOs with the public, according to a whistleblower.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_53_893646205#1_1979765291"]}, {"text": "Luis Elizondo, former head of the Advanced Aerospace Threat Identification Program (AATIP), claims to have run the program for 9 years and managed its operations out of a secretive location in the Pentagon.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_53_893646205#1_1979765291"]}, {"text": "The Advanced Aerospace Threat Identification Program (AATIP) reportedly collected and analyzed data on unexplained aerial phenomena, but specific methodologies are not detailed in the provided information.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_53_893646205#1_1979765291"]}, {"text": "Luis Elizondo claims to have generated reports supporting his claims about Unidentified Aerial Phenomena (UAP), but specific reports or studies are not mentioned in the provided information.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_53_893646205#1_1979765291"]}, {"text": "The Pentagon has reportedly established a UAP Task Force, but no new reports or findings have been released since its establishment according to the provided information.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_53_893646205#1_1979765291"]}, {"text": "Luis Elizondo's work with the AATIP program has influenced public opinion about Unidentified Aerial Phenomena (UAP), as evidenced by his claims and actions being reported in media outlets.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_53_893646205#1_1979765291"]}, {"text": "There is no mention of independent experts or organizations reviewing and validating Luis Elizondo's claims about Unidentified Aerial Phenomena (UAP) in the provided information.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_53_893646205#1_1979765291"]}, {"text": "The reports generated by the Advanced Aerospace Threat Identification Program (AATIP) do not mention any specific plans for developing new technologies based on Unidentified Aerial Phenomena (UAP).", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_53_893646205#1_1979765291"]}, {"text": "There is no mention of reports or studies generated by the AATIP program suggesting a connection between Unidentified Aerial Phenomena (UAP) and nuclear technology in the provided information.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_53_893646205#1_1979765291"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_4-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_2529216", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The Blue Whale challenge involved teenagers discussing suicide and sharing blue whale memes.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_38_230321913#1_504077088"]}, {"text": "Experts suggest psychological manipulation may be simplistic; teens drawn to forums due to mental health issues or peer pressure.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_23_248491773#1_563373615"]}, {"text": "In Russia, a high rate of adolescent suicide contributes to the spread among vulnerable youth.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_4199697#0_9230250"]}, {"text": "Russian Orthodox Church leader warned about smartphone dependence potentially bringing Antichrist, highlighting online safety concerns.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_2413955574#7_2670760147"]}, {"text": "The Blue Whale challenge was reported in Russia but not detailed in other countries.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_38_230321913#1_504077088"]}, {"text": "Governments and internet safety organizations have not taken significant steps to prevent such challenges globally.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_38_230321913#1_504077088"]}, {"text": "Experts argue the challenge might be a result of misinterpretation or manipulation of online content.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_38_230321913#1_504077088"]}, {"text": "Technology's role in shaping youth behavior and mental health is highlighted by Church leader\u2019s warning.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_2413955574#7_2670760147"]}, {"text": "Children aged 12-14 acted as 'curators' sharing shock content, indicating lack of adult manipulation.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_38_230321913#1_504077088"]}, {"text": "Rise of technology and social media platforms contributed to the Blue Whale challenge's creation and spread.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_38_230321913#1_504077088", "msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_2413955574#7_2670760147"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_4-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_7751734", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "Carlos Ghosn managed to leave Japan despite strict bail conditions, including a 24-hour camera outside his house and restrictions on technology use.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_37_618125632#7_1299675371"]}, {"text": "NHK reported that Ghosn left his house in Tokyo, walked to a nearby hotel, and then boarded a train to Osaka, where he was reportedly transported by private jet to Istanbul before reaching Beirut.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_37_618125632#7_1299675371"]}, {"text": "Ghosn's wife Carole played a significant role in his escape, speaking with him for over an hour on December 24th and meeting him upon arrival in Beirut.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_37_618125632#7_1299675371"]}, {"text": "Japanese authorities have not issued any official statements or press releases regarding their response to Ghosn's escape or future measures they plan to implement.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_37_618125632#7_1299675371"]}, {"text": "The Financial Times reported that private security operatives helped plan Ghosn's escape, with preparations reportedly spanning several months and involving multiple teams in different countries.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_37_618125632#7_1299675371"]}, {"text": "Lebanese authorities have denied any direct involvement in Ghosn's escape, with the Lebanese foreign ministry spokesperson stating that the government had no role and did not know the circumstances of his arrival.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_37_618125632#7_1299675371"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_4-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_441326441", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The National Academies of Sciences' report suggests that a microwave attack could be the most plausible explanation for Havana Syndrome symptoms, but outside experts dismiss this as implausible.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_47_1057839964#2_2289178360"]}, {"text": "Kenneth Foster from the University of Pennsylvania argues that the report does not provide a coherent argument for why microwaves should be involved in causing Havana Syndrome symptoms.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_53_989039235#4_2197708019"]}, {"text": "Mitchell Joseph Vald\u00e9s Sosa, a neuroscientist from the Cuba Neuroscience Center, disagrees with the NAS report\u2019s finding of radio frequency pulse effects and suggests psychogenic causes might be more significant.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_1479393019#1_3165849797"]}, {"text": "The NAS report recommends thorough investigations involving experts from various disciplines to study future clusters of Havana Syndrome cases, emphasizing the need for comprehensive research methods.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_17_1444328361#0_1593380088"]}, {"text": "Andrei Pakhomov, a bioengineer from Old Dominion University, questions the plausibility of microwave exposure causing Havana Syndrome symptoms based on his decades of research in the field.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_1479393019#2_3165851279"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_4-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_1300032609", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "A conservatorship is legally defined as a court case where a judge appoints an individual or organization, called the conservator, to care for someone who 'cannot care' for themselves or who cannot manage their own finances.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_880637681#9_1802064106"]}, {"text": "Jamie Spears was granted the conservatorship in 2008 after Britney purportedly struggled with mental health issues and was hospitalized, making the conservatorship permanent in 2009.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_22_1087597931#5_2423835801"]}, {"text": "Britney Spears' legal team has requested that Jodi Montgomery, a professionally licensed conservator, be named the permanent conservator of her person and that Bessemer Trust become the sole conservator of her estate.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_1292466165#1_2369928850"]}, {"text": "Jamie Spears argues that his conservatorship is working, stating that under his order, Britney's estate has gone from being in debt to having a valuation of more than $60 million.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_22_1087597931#5_2423835801"]}, {"text": "Britney Spears' legal team has expanded, with new attorneys joining her case.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_1292466165#1_2369928850"]}, {"text": "The #FreeBritney movement supports Britney's desire to leave her conservatorship, with fans staging protests and using social media to bring attention to her case.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_96496839#0_190878269"]}, {"text": "The article mentions that Bessemer Trust has been appointed as a co-conservator, but it does not provide details about their management practices or strategies in handling Britney's finances.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_1292466165#1_2369928850"]}, {"text": "Britney Spears has expanded her legal team, but the article does not explain how this change might influence the ongoing legal battles and conservatorship arrangements.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_1292466165#1_2369928850"]}, {"text": "Britney Spears' daily life and career are affected by the ongoing legal battles, but the article does not provide a clear explanation of how these events impact her personal life.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_1292466165#1_2369928850"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_4-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_38_227081897", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The article mentions that users can report videos related to the Blackout Challenge by clicking on the arrow and selecting 'report,' choosing 'suicide, self-harm, and dangerous acts.'", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_53_1353454817#1_3047770880"]}, {"text": "The article states that a 10-year-old girl from Italy died after attempting the Blackout Challenge, highlighting its dangers.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_25_500352179#1_984887400"]}, {"text": "Experts warn that participating in TikTok trends like the Blackout Challenge can lead to fainting, seizures, brain damage, or death.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_543050719#1_985327916"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_4-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_39_1014551192", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The documentary focuses on Rick Singer, the mastermind behind the largest college admissions scandal in history.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_14_83158292#2_188996314"]}, {"text": "Singer's business involved facilitating cheating on ACT and SAT exams and bribing college athletics directors with donations to their programs.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_14_83158292#2_188996314"]}, {"text": "Singer pleaded guilty to racketeering conspiracy, money laundering conspiracy, conspiracy to defraud the United States, and obstruction of justice.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_14_83158292#2_188996314"]}, {"text": "While many of the parents and college employees indicted in the scandal have been charged and sentenced, Singer is yet to be sentenced.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_14_83158292#2_188996314"]}, {"text": "The documentary does not mention any interviews with John Vandemoer, the former head coach of Stanford University sailing team.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_14_83158292#2_188996314"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_4-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_39_1165221603", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "Oxygen bars and recreational oxygen inhalers promise to improve your well-being, but the health claims are questionable.", "citations": []}, {"text": "Healthy individuals do not need extra oxygen as humans have evolved to live in an atmosphere with 21 percent oxygen.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_42_662415614#1_1371924970"]}, {"text": "While some oxygen bars and products claim to deliver up to 95 percent oxygen, they typically provide only about 35-40 percent, which is still more than the air around you but not necessarily beneficial for healthy individuals.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_38_180486736#0_381710265"]}, {"text": "The numerous health claims made by oxygen bars do not hold merit according to experts like Dr. Norman H. Edelman.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_10_621132279#3_1150828896"]}, {"text": "Using oxygen bars could pose potential health risks such as mold and bacteria growth due to lack of sterilization practices, especially for individuals with existing lung conditions.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_51_1484199789#0_3026594145"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_4-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_41_1960853470", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "Cancer researchers in Israel have found that cannabinoids can kill brain and breast cancer cells, but additional research is needed to fully understand their effectiveness.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_45_603374908#6_1083859871"]}, {"text": "Doctors at the UCSF Osher Center for Integrative Medicine caution against assuming that cannabis is a cure, citing the lack of large-scale clinical trials to support this claim.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_13_153626625#5_335444123"]}, {"text": "While anecdotal accounts suggest that some patients have experienced complete recovery after using cannabis, doctors advise against relying solely on these stories for treatment decisions.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_37_471128432#1_1003880258"]}, {"text": "The National Academies of Sciences, Engineering and Medicine found insufficient evidence to recommend cannabis as a direct treatment for cancer without large-scale clinical trials.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_45_603374908#4_1083855121"]}]}
{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_4-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_42_654618974", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "The article mentions that the Mandela Effect occurs when a large group of people believe an event occurred when it did not, citing Fiona Broome as an example.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_413093945#6_1062151918"]}, {"text": "The article suggests that false memories can explain the Mandela Effect, referencing confabulation as a possible cause.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_42724446#4_95354404"]}, {"text": "Confabulation is described as a form of honest lying where people create false memories without intending to deceive, according to the article.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_1574754246#11_3215531087"]}, {"text": "The article mentions that many examples of the Mandela Effect are close to the original or true memory, suggesting people use confabulation to fill in gaps in their own memory.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_25_476981396#14_934235322"]}, {"text": "The article notes that false memories can be a result of people recalling events differently over time, similar to the game of telephone.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_17_691675178#6_749551406"]}]}
