{"metadata": {"team_id": "TREMA_UNH", "run_id": "run_4-task-2", "topic_id": "msmarco_v2.1_doc_55_248024230", "type": "automatic", "use_starter_kit": 1}, "responses": [{"text": "Epic Games announced its lawsuit against Apple on April 15, 2020.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_36_770259359#5_1491244949"]}, {"text": "The lawsuit is part of a series of anti-competitive restraints and monopolistic practices by Apple in markets for software application distribution and processing of consumers' payments for digital content used within iOS mobile apps.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_36_770259359#5_1491244949"]}, {"text": "After Fortnite was removed from the App Store, it is still available on other platforms such as Amazon's Appstore for Android devices.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_36_770259359#5_1491244949"]}, {"text": "Epic Games claims that Apple's 30% cut from in-app purchases is unreasonable and unlawful, as it prevents them from reaching over one billion users of Apple devices unless they go through the single store controlled by Apple, the App Store.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_36_770259359#5_1491244949"]}, {"text": "The iOS version of Fortnite has generated significant revenue for Epic Games, though the exact amount is not specified in the provided documents.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_36_770259359#5_1491244949"]}, {"text": "The lawsuit mentions that other developers and companies have faced similar issues with Apple's App Store policies, indicating a broader issue within the industry.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_36_770259359#5_1491244949"]}, {"text": "Epic Games is requesting the court to take specific actions against Apple, including breaking down the App Store into smaller stores and allowing users to choose their preferred payment methods.", "citations": ["msmarco_v2.1_doc_36_770259359#5_1491244949"]}, {"text": "Tim Sweeney, CEO of Epic Games, has stated that Apple's policies stifle innovation and competition in the tech industry.", 